### Request a login code — always 202 Accepted, byte-identical for unknown emails (anti-enumeration).
### In Development the code is printed in the api console: "DEV ONLY — OTP code for ..."
POST {{host}}/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "smoke@test.local"
}


### Invalid email — 400 ValidationProblem
POST {{host}}/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email"
}


### Verify the code — 200 with accessToken; wrong/expired/replayed code — 401 Auth.InvalidCode
POST {{host}}/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "smoke@test.local",
  "code": "193737"
}


### Malformed code — 400 ValidationProblem (rejected before it can burn an attempt)
POST {{host}}/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "smoke@test.local",
  "code": "12ab"
}


### Current identity — 200 with userId when the Bearer token is valid, 401 otherwise
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
